{
  "id": "wj-06-classes",
  "region": "web-js",
  "order": 6,
  "title": "Toggle a Class",
  "story": "Instead of changing styles one by one, flip a class and let CSS do the work.",
  "goal": "Clicking #theme toggles the class dark on <body>.",
  "type": "web",
  "lang": "web",
  "starter": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n  <title>My Page</title>\n  <style>\n    body.dark { background: #111; color: #eee; }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <button id=\"theme\">Toggle</button>\n  <p>Hello</p>\n  <script>\n    // toggle the dark class on document.body\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
  "tests": [
    {
      "kind": "web",
      "label": "Starts without dark",
      "js": "return !document.body.classList.contains(\"dark\") || \"body already has dark\"",
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
      "kind": "web",
      "label": "One click adds dark",
      "js": "click(\"#theme\"); return document.body.classList.contains(\"dark\") || \"no dark class\"",
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
      "kind": "web",
      "label": "A second click removes it",
      "js": "click(\"#theme\"); return !document.body.classList.contains(\"dark\") || \"dark is still there\"",
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
      "kind": "web-clean",
      "label": "The script runs with no errors",
      "hidden": false
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "element.classList.toggle(\"name\") adds the class if missing and removes it if present.",
    "document.body.classList.toggle(\"dark\");",
    "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n  <title>My Page</title>\n  <style>\n    body.dark { background: #111; color: #eee; }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <button id=\"theme\">Toggle</button>\n  <p>Hello</p>\n  <script>\n    document.getElementById(\"theme\").addEventListener(\"click\", function () {\n      document.body.classList.toggle(\"dark\");\n    });\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
  ],
  "socratic": [
    "Why is toggling a class neater than setting colours in JS?",
    "What does toggle do on the second click?",
    "How would you only add, never remove?"
  ],
  "explain": "In one sentence: what did you learn from “Toggle a Class”?",
